# =============================================================================
# NeoDonkey — repository hygiene
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. A NeoDonkey *workspace* must never be created in this checkout.
#
# These entries are what a workspace looks like. The kernel refuses to create
# one here (see the `.neodonkey-dev` marker and the guard in runtime/kernel.js),
# and test/checkout-hygiene.test.js fails if one appears anyway. This has
# happened twice; both times it hijacked our own git history. Do not remove.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
documents/
peers/
neodonkey.json
release.json
demo-workspace/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Key material. Nothing here may ever reach a public repository.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.jwk
*.jwk.json
*.pem
*.key
release-key*
keys/
.env
.env.*

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Ordinary noise
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db

node_modules/
dist/
build/
*.log
npm-debug.log*

.idea/
.vscode/
*.sw?
.eslintcache

# Marketing, positioning and launch material live in their own repository, not here.
# This one is public and is the product: an ERP whose claims are meant to be verifiable by
# running something. Launch copy in the same tree invites a reader to treat the two as one
# kind of statement, and invites an agent to "improve" a landing page while believing it is
# working on the product. Removed 2026-08-19; see docs/journal/2026-08-19-marketing-belongs-elsewhere.md.
marketing/
